                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1199/275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-22T16:00:00-04:00">June 22, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. For Grady. Your 228, June 21, 3 p.m. It is regretted that it would be
                    contrary to the Department’s policy to permit an official of the State
                    Department to serve as substitute for you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
